  "text_input": "71-year-old female with known Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus and Systemic Hypertension for 10 years presented with loose stools up to 10 episodes, foul smelling, watery, non-blood tinged, non-mucoid since 1 day. Associated with diffuse dull aching pain abdomen worsening after stools. No vomiting, no cough, no breathlessness, no chest pain, no burning micturition. Pallor noted on examination. USG abdomen showed hepatomegaly with Grade 1 fatty liver (17cm), right renal calculi (0.3cm) and right renal complex cyst. HbA1c 10.3% indicating poorly controlled diabetes. 2D Echo showed EF 55% with sclerotic aortic valve, no RWMA, no effusion. Treated with IV antibiotics including Cefasultam (switched due to reaction), Ciprofloxacin and Metronidazole, insulin, and IV fluids. Symptoms resolved with treatment.",
